    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p27.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Vieta gives \\(p+q+r=1\\) and \\(pq+pr+qr=1.\\) Thus \\[ \\begin{aligned} p^2+q^2+r^2 &=(p+q+r)^2\\\\ &\\quad-2(pq+pr+qr)\\\\ &=-1. \\end{aligned} \\] Each root \\(t\\) satisfies \\(t^3=t^2-t+2.\\) Summing over the three roots yields \\[ p^3+q^3+r^3=-1-1+6=4. \\] This is not among choices A–D.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Use Vieta to find \\(p+q+r\\) and \\(pq+pr+qr\\)",
        "First compute \\(p^2+q^2+r^2,\\) then add the three equations satisfied by the roots"
      ],
